    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate leaning heavily into our speed-focused strategy, with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.33) and **Caleb Durbin** (68.14) serving as our primary engines. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our top overall start, capitalizing on a plus-matchup against Cavalli to maximize his elite sprint profile. Similarly, **Caleb Durbin** draws a favorable environment against Scherzer; despite the veteran arm's pedigree, the projected xERA of 5.10 and the potential for **Caleb Durbin** to exploit a slower delivery cycle make him a lock in the utility slot. **Chase Meidroth** (66.48) rounds out our top-tier plays, as his lead-off spot against Abbott and a favorable SP skill rating elevate his floor significantly. While **Christian Yelich** (64.13) requires confirmation of his #6 spot, his dynamic platoon advantage against Sasaki creates high-upside potential for a veteran who remains a staple in our daily rotation.\n\nOur most critical lineup decisions centered around maintaining efficiency while navigating specific matchup risks. **Trea Turner** (62.87) remains a mandatory start due to his stolen base prowess, though he, alongside **Kyle Schwarber** (59.89), carries a 44% rain risk that could shorten their day\u2014we are monitoring this closely. We faced a difficult choice regarding **Dillon Dingler** (55.23) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (48.46); while **Dillon Dingler** earns his spot through a strong dynamic platoon edge against Messick, **Kazuma Okamoto** sits at the lower end of our starting threshold. **Colt Keith** was the clear candidate for the final bench spot; while his park factors were favorable, his platoon disadvantage against Messick and our internal data indicating he is out of the starting lineup solidified the decision to keep him benched. As we look at the remainder of the roster, including **Gary Sanchez**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Pedro Ramirez**, and **Hector Rodriguez**, we are betting on their ability to avoid sub-40 efficiency floors and contribute to our categories while our core speed threats carry the load against susceptible pitching.",
